%% Figure 20-3 — Runtime guardrail and protected effect.
%% Message: trust is not inherited. Each boundary re-checks, and the refusal
%% happens before anything commits rather than being reported afterwards.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Agent as Agent Runtime
    participant In as Input Guardrail
    participant Pol as Policy Engine
    participant App as Approval Service
    participant Tool as Tool Gateway
    participant Sys as System of Record

    Agent->>In: proposed action + content
    In->>In: inspect untrusted content
    alt injection or policy breach detected
        In-->>Agent: refuse, nothing dispatched
    else content admissible
        In->>Pol: action, subject, resource
        Pol->>Pol: evaluate rule in scope
        alt requires human approval
            Pol->>App: request approval
            App-->>Pol: signed grant, bound to this proposal
        end
        Pol-->>Tool: authorized invocation
        Tool->>Tool: check idempotency ledger
        Tool->>Sys: commit once
        Sys-->>Tool: receipt
        Tool-->>Agent: effect record + evidence
    end
